{"posts":[{"id":"hs_p73_1801","t":"Hello Hoeschec, When you are refining your kink to the LTF for a better entry, you need to still put your stop loss behind the original size kink you have identified initially in the higher time frame. This will prevent you from getting stopped out.","a":"Atari","d":"","n":"#1801","p":73,"im":[],"m":1801},{"id":"hs_p73_1802","t":"EUR-CHF Basic Practice:","a":"hoeschec","d":"","n":"#1802","p":73,"im":["173d59198b91888e5e0ec577b53037c621838b09","9f6f8ea0c902552231ffd4843682dfcdb488202c"],"m":1802},{"id":"hs_p73_1803","t":"gslao wrote: Hello Hoeschec, When you are refining your kink to the LTF for a better entry, you need to still put your stop loss behind the original size kink you have identified initially in the higher time frame. This will prevent you from getting stopped out.\n\nPerfect! Thanks for your help!","a":"hoeschec","d":"","n":"#1803","p":73,"im":[],"m":1803},{"id":"hs_p73_1804","t":"Closely analyzing setups to find out why price bounces at certain levels...and misses others.\n\nThis is an interesting example on EUR-AUD:\n\nHourly Chart:\n\nWhen I first traded this on simulation, I chose a different kink. My analysis is shown below:\n\nI didn't even see the IQM...even though it was right in my face.. I was too focused on the PA below...tunnel vision can be very damaging to a trading career.","a":"hoeschec","d":"","n":"#1804","p":73,"im":["9bdc8b5b1135a0995f0feba23d70c6b480b19e64","22b993201fdff02b661d6174a420b205c319719f","3a3cc13837be3decbbd214e6ab0b93a447b5c836","6762a6f21b06b34cc5aeb0f4942bfe85ef16109d","a434a6b45adf823e6350ac7390c74ef865752541","496608afc49d665cc7eaf8882cf88e8db3545313"],"m":1804},{"id":"hs_p73_1805","t":"EUR-AUD Continued:\n\nVery similar PA forms above the initial trade. This time however, price did not make a substantial high, so there was no trade opportunity.","a":"hoeschec","d":"","n":"#1805","p":73,"im":["5bbdff579bcfb1dc841fcaa388922df379dac358"],"m":1805},{"id":"hs_p73_1806","t":"EUR-AUD:\n\nHere is a failed trade... similar analysis but this time no bounce at the kink.\n\nIt seems (from my homework) the best kink reactions occur hidden inside a 1-hour candle after price has made a substantial high/low. In this case, price does form a large bearish candle with momentum, but the downside flow through was limited before price came back to the kink.\n\nMore 'space between' the new low/high and the associated kink seems to mean better bounces. The last chart posted below shows what I mean by 'space between'.","a":"hoeschec","d":"","n":"#1806","p":73,"im":["16cc23af07da0260e1a42d93cb1f44feac70bbd7","a02b3441f43378c976d41d86120271594e0d6394","3cb78c8e567f73bddcb2f36ff3f439d1aabcae97"],"m":1806},{"id":"hs_p73_1807","t":"EUR-AUD Simulation Trade:\n\nI like the bearish momentum bar show below:\n\nTwo Fakeouts above, both hit targets. This tells me price is coming from a met target for longs. I am looking for a place to get short.\n\nLS is chosen as labeled below:\n\nNow I will look at the lower time frames to identify the best entry with the lowest risk:\n\nI will draw the LS Kink from 30-min charts down to 1-min.\n\n30-Minute Chart:\n\n15-Minute Chart:\n\n5-Minute Chart:\n\n1-Min Chart:\n\nI will use the 1-min chart as the basis for the short trade, but I will keep all scales in mind when it comes to my stop loss. The 1-min FTR is approximately 20 pips wide. The 5-min kink increases substantially to over 90 pips. This is way too wide...I will have to refine my entry. There is a wick on the 1-min chart that looks like a good place for a reaction - I will be sure to place my stop beyond the extreme of this wick.\n\nStill, the risk is too high on this (for me). From the beginning of the FTR to the extent of the wick, is approximately 30 Pips. To minimize the risk, I will set my entry order higher up in the FTR. Doing this may end in me missing the reaction, but I have to manage my risk. My entry order will be the green dotted line on the chart below.\n\n- Risk is approximately 20 Pips, I am looking for a minimum of 3:R\n\nTrade is a winner - but almost got stopped out:","a":"hoeschec","d":"","n":"#1807","p":73,"im":["f181af5af24eb91ce7e40ffe26e9a2f7e07beacf","1746ee4765fe68204a4a7c563c3974688f755c0f","f46ee642f3288a382b77ae987bbc73aa610f1c19","4776e8cc4a6bc437d89a444e2ee9d1620b072b23","9543e8cd27a6d1083293c465bd979c1913ca6548","7407a42b67067ec4272d39e780d177c0ff5f6c0f","d459774988adad6e55400f983ab3e8676a6edae1"],"m":1807},{"id":"hs_p73_1808","t":"I wasn't in time to catch this one on USD-CAD but it is a perfect example Simulation:","a":"hoeschec","d":"","n":"#1808","p":73,"im":["1131f7f82394575a179de21de9ffd3058b4fceac","643fba15951de84a83bb034c3338844697f83188"],"m":1808},{"id":"hs_p73_1809","t":"Just closed Simulation trade USD-CAD:\n\nThis was a small scalp because the higher time frame showed that price was likely just faking out to the downside..any short taken at kink should be carefully monitored.\n\nIn this case, the risk was low and there was enough upside to make the RR acceptable.\n\nLow Time Frame:","a":"hoeschec","d":"","n":"#1809","p":73,"im":["92f98d95b90a5aba77d80ed2c19b742f6c9069b3","f61644fe16964124818f0db20dbfbd099ac61643","519215f0ddd474a4fa5039484e7762594891444d"],"m":1809},{"id":"hs_p73_1810","t":"Hi, Took a look at your trade, and if I understand it correctly you don't wait for PA to enter, you try to understand how are the reactions to the kinks you draw?","a":"HCDE","d":"","n":"#1810","p":73,"im":[],"m":1810},{"id":"hs_p73_1811","t":"HCDE wrote: Hi, Took a look at your trade, and if I understand it correctly you don't wait for PA to enter, you try to understand how are the reactions to the kinks you draw?\n\nHi HDCE,\n\nThanks for stopping by my journal. I don't always look for PA prior to entering at a kink, although waiting for a LTF DM in to a HTF kink is my favorite kind of setup\n\nMost of my trades are touch trades...I focus on finding the correct kink based on the correct LS.\n\nThe best kinks are hidden in larger time frame candles.","a":"hoeschec","d":"","n":"#1811","p":73,"im":[],"m":1811},{"id":"hs_p73_1812","t":"","a":"hoeschec","d":"","n":"#1812","p":73,"im":["417767a1e02a68292a2f99dbc3ac0d4ac00c7fb7"],"m":1812},{"id":"hs_p73_1813","t":"Thinking a lot about IQM's lately.\n\nHow does an IQM happen? How can IT's ignore levels?\n\nDo they place huge orders over a short amount of time to cause a gap in pricing?\n\nWhere do they place these orders?\n\nLet's assume $100M of sell orders exists here. When price reaches the QM level it will bounce as long as there is less than $100M worth of buyers at that moment. If there is more than $100M of buyers price will consume the sell orders and price will rise. Price must consume the short orders before it can move beyond the level, right?\n\nHow are IT's able to 'skip over' these areas?\n\nIf IT's want to skip the level they need to create more buy orders. This causes price to move up. The theory behind trading the IQM (as I understand it) is price bounces at a previously ignored level because residual orders exist. But how can there be residual orders...aren't those orders consumed when price moves through the zone?\n\nMaybe IT's create huge Buy orders to cause a gap to occur? If price changes rapidly there will be gap...trapping traders who can't execute quick enough.\n\nTo me, it seems like an IQM really just a liquidity gap that fills at a later date?\n\nHow do we define an IQM? What is the difference between a DM and an IQM? What if price comes close to the QM level but falls just short of the level. Does this count as a IQM? Often times price will miss the QM level by a few pips...do we still count this as an IQM?\n\nDuring IF's video, he mentions \"IQM\" when there is no valid QM...I think there is a difference between an IQM and a IHS (Ignored head and shoulders). QM's have an engulf whereas H&S does not.\n\nWhich one of the drawings below depicts a valid IQM?","a":"hoeschec","d":"","n":"#1813","p":73,"im":["3fef4f616dd90be59879026c817ee6e084d7a79f","dda2eccd5e7acbd3ec92534c1728e240554ed504"],"m":1813},{"id":"hs_p73_1814","t":"EUR-JPY:\n\nHTF momentum candle:","a":"hoeschec","d":"","n":"#1814","p":73,"im":["63e665fc400299325df1b98b8496ce235cc8b60d","1a8ce84a98829df6fb1fdf51017e7f8844c2e4ac","c7a4f3255e6c18f05ad289d6cc312f078444ac08","5a9d4cf8a6349c0d86d11fa96168c7b0ed2ec399"],"m":1814},{"id":"hs_p73_1815","t":"EUR-JPY Detailed Setup:\n\nLooking for large momentum candles on the 15-Min chart and came across this:\n\nAsk: where is price likely to RT? Start by drawing important areas of the chart.\n\nClose up 1-min chart:","a":"hoeschec","d":"","n":"#1815","p":73,"im":["f7b7be9f13c307917e059552e097d7ada791054b","c7551de8e4ff7cd5d5b24ee4abfc85ccf51e7bc9","4c9eddf551a2e6ca8e9c8e17ddf9afa75603bcc3","f29ae6f2e089d2e04fc9b767ac89c0279643b373"],"m":1815},{"id":"hs_p73_1816","t":"USD-JPY Simulation:","a":"hoeschec","d":"","n":"#1816","p":73,"im":["b30539712224ac2d5c3e4dc470f0664ffe416ac8","2219c71f54942721d16fb4e81b7008ba9b575af7"],"m":1816},{"id":"hs_p73_1817","t":"USD-JPY","a":"hoeschec","d":"","n":"#1817","p":73,"im":["0d52fa18bd6eafaf29910663e556b97905f3440b","db608c52a902b3b73c60ca29438a8c07bfe7df5e"],"m":1817},{"id":"hs_p73_1818","t":"USD-JPY:","a":"hoeschec","d":"","n":"#1818","p":73,"im":["fce140bfc1baed178a33a4d3bff1cfc5e368b145","61afc1136f3832239cbc76ed1b5d9fb100c61033","25368fbc58ee863d29d10abbb916e392032cde62","ca843977028a1e6e031c1b3a9cc249097a4c23f3"],"m":1818},{"id":"hs_p73_1819","t":"USD-JPY Simulation - Stopped Out\n\nGreat example of multiple areas of confluence, wide area of potential areas for price to bounce. Trades like this are inevitable, the important thing to remember is minimize loss and remain disciplined.","a":"hoeschec","d":"","n":"#1819","p":73,"im":["c8d0eea9091049a2c692f6922a2a1dbb84dc708e","000fb540040138a812965939fbfcaea64c03735c","ed2c305dd3112f74f90883f18594223d2226f2c7"],"m":1819},{"id":"hs_p73_1820","t":"USD-JPY Simulation:","a":"hoeschec","d":"","n":"#1820","p":73,"im":["d9366bdbb7cf8b4246f945becd39eaa4c221492f","53cb9472fc5280cebddf77ec001d7dfdcc64a43d","8a41ff2cd1c41e92360957112ff2041966ac6e53"],"m":1820},{"id":"hs_p73_1821","t":"USD-JPY:\n\nReally nice example- Forward testing simulation:","a":"hoeschec","d":"","n":"#1821","p":73,"im":["7176f810679c099fa891009449d69bc8b1e75a50","490c48f81eca98d7ffbd8a67bdb54c2c0f0f5fd6","fe15c030d2a445a69c74c172aeee84754fc9a247"],"m":1821},{"id":"hs_p73_1822","t":"Some drawings I made today\n\nIf I want to enter a long trade at the location indicated on the drawings, I want to buy at the best price possible. I wan to buy in the direction of the valid engulf. A valid engulf is an engulf that has yet to hit its target. Usually it is challenging to determine whether PA is depicting a FO or an EG. If I buy at the location indicated in my drawing, I need to make sure price is coming from an unmet target for longs.\n\nIn all of my drawings there is a grey line labeled \"Opposing Zone\". I think it is important to define what this opposing zone should be, in terms of the formation of a LS. My understanding (although I might be wrong) is a valid LS is formed after it engulfs a UFL/LFL. In this case, it shows price engulfing an opposing UFL.","a":"hoeschec","d":"","n":"#1822","p":73,"im":["e694c7f181bbea2f9d827213b0249d0e189c9954","78723234a8746169ee6762b56a8e7976fcf06405","f71dabc51cc2560740f574d260aaf2a35cd256aa","f41f54979b912fa822b38161df98db0182eb7345"],"m":1822},{"id":"hs_p73_1823","t":"This is a repeat of a UJ simulation trade I analyzed a few days ago. I am back to this example because it helps me focus on the right kind of setup. I am finding it's helpful to keep a collection of perfect trades so when your mind becomes scrambled you can 'center' yourself.\n\nThis is my stabilizing trade:\n\nBasics:","a":"hoeschec","d":"","n":"#1823","p":73,"im":["7d9a0403c73d494b08dd4157bd8287a4eaa40fee","3c45898f09794f6e3f2a3971206207108389ac10","3a7479bee86c61e8a2d824d805c2d8008486e1e4"],"m":1823},{"id":"hs_p73_1824","t":"Taking a closer look at this USD-JPY Trade. The more I Iook, the more I see:\n\nIf anyone sees something I missed please feel free to let me know!\n\n1. Kink of LS #5 2. Established range, created by the kink formed at #1 3. Another LS forms, as final LS formed prior to a break of range #2 4. Strong momentum candle breaks range # 2\n\nA - Engulf\n\n5. LS 6. RBD 7. Another LTF IQM formed as price breaks through 8. Demand formed, creating a nice level to FO at a later time 9. \"High\" portion of a partially formed bullish QM 10. Engulf above established RS (# 9), and the \"Higher High\" Portion of the partially formed bullish QM\n\nB - The entry long occurs at the important kink (hidden in large momentum candle to the left) and at the same time forms a DM.\n\nMy focus this week will be establishing a list of paramaters that I will use as a checklist to guide my decision making process. There will be two main kinds of parameters:\n\n1. Parameters that must exist in order for me to take a trade 2. Parameters that specify 'aspects' of PA that can't exist in order for me to take a trade","a":"hoeschec","d":"","n":"#1824","p":73,"im":["ddd98fb377865dca16e7907361900662e36036b2"],"m":1824},{"id":"hs_p73_1825","t":"Nice observations H.\n\nBut for me to cope in real time with all this information going on my brain starts to shut down, I think maybe it´s better atleast for me to focus on 1 or 2 setups and learn to master these. How do you deal with all this information in your above chart and would you have been able to pull the trigger at the right moment? Just looking for opinions on how people propcess all this info and hopefully make the right desision\n\n686970717273747576","a":"hansma","d":"","n":"#1825","p":73,"im":[],"m":1825}],"images":[{"k":"173d59198b91888e5e0ec577b53037c621838b09","t":"assets/thumbs/173d59198b91888e5e0ec577b53037c621838b09.webp","f":"assets/images/173d59198b91888e5e0ec577b53037c621838b09.png","w":1800,"h":904,"b":356814,"o":"173d59198b91888e5e0ec577b53037c621838b09.png","p":73,"pid":"hs_p73_1802"},{"k":"9f6f8ea0c902552231ffd4843682dfcdb488202c","t":"assets/thumbs/9f6f8ea0c902552231ffd4843682dfcdb488202c.webp","f":"assets/images/9f6f8ea0c902552231ffd4843682dfcdb488202c.png","w":1800,"h":894,"b":388565,"o":"9f6f8ea0c902552231ffd4843682dfcdb488202c.png","p":73,"pid":"hs_p73_1802"},{"k":"9bdc8b5b1135a0995f0feba23d70c6b480b19e64","t":"assets/thumbs/9bdc8b5b1135a0995f0feba23d70c6b480b19e64.webp","f":"assets/images/9bdc8b5b1135a0995f0feba23d70c6b480b19e64.png","w":1800,"h":904,"b":458640,"o":"9bdc8b5b1135a0995f0feba23d70c6b480b19e64.png","p":73,"pid":"hs_p73_1804"},{"k":"22b993201fdff02b661d6174a420b205c319719f","t":"assets/thumbs/22b993201fdff02b661d6174a420b205c319719f.webp","f":"assets/images/22b993201fdff02b661d6174a420b205c319719f.png","w":1800,"h":901,"b":369249,"o":"22b993201fdff02b661d6174a420b205c319719f.png","p":73,"pid":"hs_p73_1804"},{"k":"3a3cc13837be3decbbd214e6ab0b93a447b5c836","t":"assets/thumbs/3a3cc13837be3decbbd214e6ab0b93a447b5c836.webp","f":"assets/images/3a3cc13837be3decbbd214e6ab0b93a447b5c836.png","w":1800,"h":898,"b":446518,"o":"3a3cc13837be3decbbd214e6ab0b93a447b5c836.png","p":73,"pid":"hs_p73_1804"},{"k":"6762a6f21b06b34cc5aeb0f4942bfe85ef16109d","t":"assets/thumbs/6762a6f21b06b34cc5aeb0f4942bfe85ef16109d.webp","f":"assets/images/6762a6f21b06b34cc5aeb0f4942bfe85ef16109d.png","w":1800,"h":895,"b":498312,"o":"6762a6f21b06b34cc5aeb0f4942bfe85ef16109d.png","p":73,"pid":"hs_p73_1804"},{"k":"a434a6b45adf823e6350ac7390c74ef865752541","t":"assets/thumbs/a434a6b45adf823e6350ac7390c74ef865752541.webp","f":"assets/images/a434a6b45adf823e6350ac7390c74ef865752541.png","w":1800,"h":892,"b":408455,"o":"a434a6b45adf823e6350ac7390c74ef865752541.png","p":73,"pid":"hs_p73_1804"},{"k":"496608afc49d665cc7eaf8882cf88e8db3545313","t":"assets/thumbs/496608afc49d665cc7eaf8882cf88e8db3545313.webp","f":"assets/images/496608afc49d665cc7eaf8882cf88e8db3545313.png","w"